  "details": "I use the buttons in nearly every crowded instance I am in to un-show people I've manually shown. They are useful to quickly scan through every single person in the instance. \n\nThere are 2 solutions to this: \n\n1.) Put the the forwards/backwards buttons back in the Quick Menu.\n\n2.) Add a \"safety\" page in the here menu that lets me easily reset the settings I have for **only the people actively in that instance**. (or even just a single button for it \"Reset all shown avatars\")\n\nTo be clear, adding a button to reset all safety settings across everyone on my account is **not** what this is for. (I believe you can already do this on the website)\n\nThe goal here is to reset the manually shown avatars in the instance. So far, the way I usually find fastest to do this is via those forward/backward buttons. That is the #2 thing I use the profile menu for, right after enabling people's avatars. It'd also be awesome to have it for non-friends or non-favorites but that's creepin the scope. \n\nI just want to be able to quickly see who I do/don't have manually shown in the instance, and quickly reset them to use safety settings. \n\nThe functionality already exists, please consider adding the buttons back! And if it turns out the buttons are still there, let me put them at the top please!\n\nEDIT: I see in the Q & A it mentions being able to switch back to the old look, that's nice! Hopefully the buttons get added to the new UI, it looks great and I wanna use it! (or maybe we get a customizable UI, pwetty pwease VRC let us pay for it)\n\nEDIT 2: I triple-checked and I don't see a New Look category, even under Open Beta. Perhaps I was too quick? Sowwie moderators",
